<h4 class="comment-title"><a title="no subject" href="52172.html@thread=324300#cmt324300" class=" invisible" >no subject</a></h4><span class="datetime"><span class="comment-date-text">Date: </span> <span title="3 days after journal entry">2026-07-16 05:16 am (UTC)</span></span></div>
</div>
<div class="contents">
<div class="inner">
<div class="userpic"></div>
<span class="poster comment-poster"><span class="comment-from-text">From:</span> <span lj:user="transitional_writes" style="white-space: nowrap;" class="ljuser"><a href="profile"><img src="https://www.dreamwidth.org/img/silk/identity/user.png" alt="[personal profile] " width="17" height="17" style="vertical-align: text-bottom; border: 0; padding-right: 1px;" /></a><a href="index.html"><b>transitional_writes</b></a></span></span>
<span class="poster-ip"><span class="comment-ip-text">IP Address:</span> (51.178.141.131)</span><div class="comment-content">Let's play a simple game.<br />We can try to understand something complex from the scratch.<br /><br />A lot of people are interesting in the Linux from scratch.<br /><a href="https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/">https://www.linuxfromscratch.org/</a><br /><br />A lot of people is building old or original small computers from scratch<br /><a href="https://github.com/wieker/electrolyser/tree/master/fpga/based6502/hx1k-6502/verilog-6502">https://github.com/wieker/electrolyser/tree/master/fpga/based6502/hx1k-6502/verilog-6502</a><br /><br />There is nothing impossible or special to understand something from scratch.<br /><br />But what is the beginning?<br />Let's base our understanding on mathematics, algorithm theory and real formal computer security.<br />That is beginning with the questions.<br />1. How many soldiers are guarding the software developer which software you use.<br />2. Are you observing and control all those soldiers all the time? If not - don't use this software.<br /><a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solomonoff%27s_theory_of_inductive_inference">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Solomonoff%27s_theory_of_inductive_inference</a><br /><br />And what is our questions?<br />Let's start with the following two questions.<br />1. How to achieve minimum garbage production with the economic current consumption level.<br />2. How with the current garbage production achieve higher economic consumption level.<br /><br />What is our method?<br />In the age of digital photo and IP cameras you can assume that there is one virtual camera for each man leaving on the earth.<br />In the age of software development you can ask each software developer to write POV ray scripts or<br />other software that will render all the things he saw in the life.<br /><br />You can check your own POV ray scripts for errors.<br />But how to check others? What scenario is most probable?<br /><br />We can use Occam's razor: the most simple scenario is most probable one.<br />This is so called apriory Solomonoff distribuition.<br /><br />So how to answer on our question about how to compare garbage production if you don't see<br />garbage and don't have gold money to calculate it?<br /><br />Just believe other people.<br />But this just move this question to other people.<br />How he is comparing garbage?<br /><br />And there is no other answer for it.<br />Because everything that you will see will be<br />1. physics: garbage and gold<br />2. other people that are talking something.<br /><br />But how gold money can help to compare garbage?<br /><br />The limits of production R1, R2 -&gt; R3 are restricted by<br />the budget that you have.<br />To increase budget you have to sell R3 with profit.<br />If you are producing more garbage then your competitor<br />he will get more money than you and will replace you on the market.<br /><br />You have to use production processes that produce less garbage.<br /><br />If you don't use mathematical proofs and gold for garbage calculation<br />but believe other people you will get infinite recursive chain of garbage<br />producers.<div class='edittime'><em>Edited <span class="datetime"><span class="comment-date-text">Date: </span> <span title="">2026-07-16 06:06 am (UTC)</span></span></em></div></div></div>
